h </c><00:00:00.936><c>tier  </c><00:00:00.937><c>4 </c><00:00:00.938><c>d </c><00:00:00.939><c>are </c><00:00:00.940><c>there </c><00:00:00.941><c>any </c><00:00:00.942><c>other </c><00:00:00.943><c>tips </c><00:00:00.944><c>you </c><00:00:00.945><c>thought  </c><00:00:00.946><c>of </c><00:00:00.947><c>that </c><00:00:00.948><c>might </c><00:00:00.949><c>help </c><00:00:00.950><c>out </c><00:00:00.951><c>fellow </c><00:00:00.952><c>travelers  </c><00:00:00.953><c>leave </c><00:00:00.954><c>them </c><00:00:00.955><c>in </c><00:00:00.956><c>the </c><00:00:00.957><c>comments </c><00:00:00.958><c>below </c><00:00:00.959><c>and  </c><00:00:00.960><c>thank </c><00:00:00.961><c>you </c><00:00:00.962><c>so </c><00:00:00.963><c>much </c><00:00:00.964><c>for </c><00:00:00.965><c>watching  </c><00:00:00.966><c>[Music]  </c><00:00:00.967><c>you  </c><00:00:00.968><c>[Music]</c>

00:00:01.819 --> 00:00:04.130 align:start position:0%
welcome to the wonderful and dreary  world of greed fall where you play as a  user created character and a fantastical  version of the seventeenth century  throughout your adventure you'll explore  a remote island chat with natives and  grow your influence as you attempt to  cure a mysterious illness the skills  attributes and abilities your character  has are yours to choose but if you're  feeling a bit overwhelmed by it all  we're here to help you get off to a good  start here are seven tips to hit the  ground running in greed fall number one  talents act as skill checks like most  role-playing games greed fall has its  fair share of skill trees when you start  your adventure you will need to pick a  talent these include charisma science  intuition vigor craftsmanship and  lock-picking these essentially act as  skill checks as you level up you'll be  able to invest in each of these trees  however keep in mind that you will only  have one talent point to spend at the  beginning this means there are certain  options and areas will be locked out of  in the beginning of greed fall for  example the owner of a bar wants you to  fix his furniture or give him money to  repair it based on what your cousin has  done if you do not have craftsmanship  level 1 then you can't really repair  them despite being allowed to pick that  option you can reset your points with  memory crystals but you won't have a ton  of those in the beginning keep these  things in mind when deciding which  talents you choose number to focus on  lock-picking  while all of these talents are useful we  found that there are a lot of locked  doors in chests in the first area of the  city of serene and because you won't be  able to return to serene after the  tutorial you probably won't want to miss  out on the extra items and loot hidden  and locked chests there are also some  runes you happen upon rather early in  the game and you're required to open  three chests to continue through them so  if you don't have the lock picking skill  or some spare keys then you'll have to  backtrack or reset your talents focus on  the pistol two swords or cool button  greed for the pistol is way better  pistols can do a ton of damage to enemy  armor and can knock foes back pistols  are also useful against enemy  ceil encounter swords don't do nearly as  much damage and sometimes they can't  even penetrate enemy armor you can buy  pistol ammo from merchants so make sure  you're stocked up I'd also recommend  leveling up the pistol skills sooner  rather than later number four don't  discredit your teammates in some games  your teammates suck and don't do much  for you however in greed fall I'd argue  your teammates can sometimes be better  than you I've been in situations where  my team and I have been ambushed by four  to five monsters and my teammates took  care of the majority of them keep this  in mind when deciding who you want on  your team and how you want to build your  relationship with them you'll be able to  check their skills attributes and other  details about them before picking them -  just a heads up that you can only have  two people on your party at a time  so pick wisely number 5 look for  campsites the island of Tier four D is  massive and it can take a while to get  from point A to point B fortunately  there is fast travel as you explore the  world keep an eye out for camp sites  these act as hubs that let you swap out  your gear rest and of course fast travel  when you first land in Tier four D  you'll get a quest that will ask you to  map the island by finding campsites and  other points of interest this is a good  way to track how many camp sites are in  each area keep in mind that you can't  fast travel at any time you need to be  at a camp or a globe number six loyalty  missions taken right out of a Bioware  game greed fall features loyalty  missions  these are personal quests designed  specifically around one of your  teammates upon completing one of these  quests your bond with that teammate will  increase you'll want to keep these bonds  high because if you piss off a friend  too much they might abandon your crew  altogether so make sure to check on your  teammates often number seven fury and  tactical pause combat can be tough and  greed fall especially if you're under  leveled  however there are some techniques and  strategies you'll want to know first pay  attention to your fury meter as you cast  spells attack and counter you'll build  fury you can then unleash your fury by  pulling right trigger this move deals a  significant amount of damage and can  knock your enemies off balance  greed fall also has something called  tactical pause this allows you to pause  combat and let you pick your next move  you probably won't need to use this all  that often but we found it useful during  the trickier fights if you need to heal  or pick the right spell use tactical  pause hopefully these tips helped you  get started on your journey through tier  4 d are there any other tips you thought  of that might help out fellow travelers  leave them in the comments below and  thank you so much for watching  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

